f:["$","p",null,{"children":["The store's ",["$","em",null,{"children":"type"}]," is whichever key you put inside its object:\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"filesystem"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"memory"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"compression"}],", ",["$","code",null,{"children":"fast_slow"}],", and so on. Forge\npicks the implementation from that key; everything else in the object is\nthat implementation's config. The set of legal keys is the variant list of a\nsingle enum, so the reference below and the parser cannot disagree."]}]
